{"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t# recsys — arXiv paper recommender\n2\t\n3\tLearns my historical \"is this paper worth reading?\" filter from ~9 months of recorded triage\n4\t(`papers_seen` ⊃ `papers_downloaded` ⊃ `papers_kept`) and surfaces a ranked top-N of new papers.\n5\t\n6\tApproach: a **frozen** text-embedding backbone + a tiny trainable head, with **cascade** inference\n7\t(title ranker scores all candidates → top-K → fetch abstracts → abstract ranker → top-N).\n8\tFull design and rationale: [`../RECOMMENDER_DESIGN.md`](../RECOMMENDER_DESIGN.md).\n9\t\n10\t## Ground-truth safety\n11\t\n12\tThe three funnel CSVs and the legacy scripts at the repo root are **read-only ground truth**.\n13\tNothing in `recsys/` writes to them. Every generated artifact goes into a separate, git-ignored tree:\n14\t\n15\t| Path | Contents |\n16\t|---|---|\n17\t| `data/clean/stage{1,2}.parquet` | Labeled, deduped, temporally-split training tables (C1) |\n18\t| `data/abstracts/abstracts.jsonl` | Abstract cache, one JSON record per line (C2) |\n19\t| `data/embeddings/{model}/{field}.npy` | Cached embedding vectors + row-aligned `.ids.json` index (C3) |\n20\t| `models/stage{1,2}/` | Winning head (`head.joblib`) + `metadata.json` (backbone, val metrics, N) (C4) |\n21\t| `data/digests/digest_<date>.md` | Top-N markdown preview of an inference run (C5) |\n22\t| `data/digests/candidates_<date>.csv` | **Full** ranked candidate pool the review UIs read (C5) |\n23\t| `state/seen_ids.txt`, `state/last_run.json` | Incremental-run seen-set + watermark |\n24\t| `state/feedback.jsonl` | Your keep/skip decisions from the review UIs (C6 training source) |\n25\t\n26\t## Setup\n27\t\n28\tThe repo's old top-level `venv/` is stale (its interpreter path no longer resolves). This package\n29\tuses its own `.venv`:\n30\t\n31\t```bash\n32\tpython3 -m venv .venv\n33\t.venv/bin/python -m pip install -e .      # deps pinned in pyproject.toml / requirements-recsys.txt\n34\t```\n35\t\n36\t## Usage\n37\t\n38\tRun modules from the repo root with the package venv:\n39\t\n40\t```bash\n41\t# C1 — build the training tables (reads the CSVs, writes data/clean/*.parquet)\n42\t.venv/bin/python -m recsys.dataset            # --val-weeks N to change the temporal holdout\n43\t\n44\t# C2 — backfill abstracts for the ~1,817 downloaded IDs (resumable; re-runs are network-free)\n45\t.venv/bin/python -m recsys.abstracts          # --limit N for a quick smoke test\n46\t\n47\t# C3 — embed titles (stage 1) + title+abstract (stage 2); cached, incremental, re-runs are no-ops\n48\t.venv/bin/python -m recsys.embeddings         # --model NAME, --stage 1|2|both, --no-title\n49\t\n50\t# C4 — train + evaluate the heads as rankers on the temporal val split (full bake-off)\n51\t#   requires both backbones cached first (bge default + the old-encoder baseline):\n52\t.venv/bin/python -m recsys.embeddings --model sentence-transformers/bert-base-nli-mean-tokens\n53\t.venv/bin/python -m recsys.train              # --stage 1|2|both, --old-backbone NAME\n54\t\n55\t# C5 — incremental fetch -> cascade score -> ranked digest (data/digests/), advance state\n56\t.venv/bin/python -m recsys.infer              # first run: last 7 days\n57\t.venv/bin/python -m recsys.infer --dry-run --top-n 30 # score + digest, don't touch seen-set/watermark\n58\t# big backlog: date-windowed + resumable. If arXiv 429s or you stop it, re-run the\n59\t# SAME command — completed windows (state/backlog.json) are skipped, no re-querying.\n60\t# Convenience wrapper (CPU embeddings, caffeinate, logs to state/backlog_run.log):\n61\tzsh scripts/run_backlog.sh        # run late-night; re-run to resume until complete\n62\t\n63\t# C5 review — record keep/skip decisions (expand-to-distinguish; feeds C6 retraining)\n64\t.venv/bin/python -m recsys.review             # terminal interface (latest candidates file)\n65\t\n66\t# C5 download — after filtering, fetch PDFs for everything you kept into pdfs-to-summarize/\n67\t.venv/bin/python -m recsys.download           # idempotent (skip-existing); --dry-run to preview\n68\t\n69\t# tests (no network)\n70\t.venv/bin/python recsys/tests/test_ids.py\n71\t.venv/bin/python recsys/tests/test_abstracts_cache.py\n72\t.venv/bin/python recsys/tests/test_embeddings_cache.py\n73\t.venv/bin/python recsys/tests/test_ranking_metrics.py\n74\t.venv/bin/python recsys/tests/test_infer.py\n75\t.venv/bin/python recsys/tests/test_feedback.py\n76\t.venv/bin/python recsys/tests/test_download.py\n77\t```\n78\t\n79\t## Module map\n80\t\n81\t| Module | Component | Role |\n82\t|---|---|---|\n83\t| `ids.py` | C0 | `arxiv_id()` — robust ID extraction (modern, legacy, version-strip; `None` for non-arXiv) |\n84\t| `arxiv_client.py` | C0 | `ArxivClient` — batched `id_list` fetch, whole-chunk retries, per-ID fallback, `on_batch` hook |\n85\t| `io_csv.py` | C0 | Load the funnel CSVs into deduped, ID-keyed frames; verify the nesting invariant |\n86\t| `state.py` | C0 | Incremental-run seen-set + watermark (`state/`) |\n87\t| `dataset.py` | C1 | Build `stage{1,2}.parquet` — date recovery, labels, temporal split, unread-batch exclusion |\n88\t| `abstracts.py` | C2 | Abstract cache + backfill (`data/abstracts/abstracts.jsonl`) |\n89\t| `embeddings.py` | C3 | Frozen-backbone embeddings, cached per `(model, field)`; incremental append + request-order alignment |\n90\t| `train.py` | C4 | Train logreg/MLP heads + TF-IDF/trivial baselines; rank metrics on the temporal val split; save winner. Also `score_texts()` — the inference dispatch C5 reuses |\n91\t| `infer.py` | C5 | Incremental/windowed fetch (categories−blacklist, watermark) → cascade score → ranked md + full-pool CSV → advance seen-set+watermark |\n92\t| `review.py` | C5 | Terminal review UI + `ReviewSession` core (load candidates, record keep/skip decisions) |\n93\t| `download.py` | C5 | Fetch PDFs for kept papers (`feedback.kept_papers()`) into `pdfs-to-summarize/`; idempotent |\n94\t| `feedback.py` | C5/C6 | Decision event log (`state/feedback.jsonl`) + `derive_labels()` → stage-1/stage-2 training rows |\n95\t\n96\t## Notes / gotchas\n97\t\n98\t- **Join only on arXiv ID, never title** (titles are mangled). `arxiv_id()` is the single\n99\t  chokepoint for that.\n100\t- **`papers_downloaded.csv`'s `Paper Date` is corrupt** (stores the run date); the true date is\n101\t  recovered by joining to `papers_seen.csv`.\n102\t- **arXiv's `UnexpectedEmptyPageError`** is raised mid-iteration on a flaky empty first page; the\n103\t  client materializes each chunk inside a retry so results never silently truncate to zero.\n104\t- **numpy 2.5 × pandas 2.3:** `pd.Timedelta(days=N)` trips a generic-unit deprecation — use\n105\t  `pd.DateOffset(...)` for date arithmetic.\n106\t- **C4 finding — TF-IDF is a strong baseline.** In the bake-off, TF-IDF+logreg matches or beats\n107\t  the modern embedding backbone on the temporal val split (stage-1 AUC **0.838** vs bge **0.810**;\n108\t  competitive on stage-2). Embeddings do **not** obviously win here. The saved `models/` winner is\n109\t  still the best *embedding* head (the locked cascade design embeds live candidates), but TF-IDF is\n110\t  a viable — and far lighter — alternative worth revisiting. Stage-2 metrics are weak (AUC ~0.67)\n111\t  and noisy: val is only 244 rows / 26 pos.\n112\t- **Whole pipeline trains in ~20s on the Air CPU** — heads are tiny; the backbone is frozen and\n113\t  its embeddings are cached, so retraining (C6) is effectively free.\n114\t- **Review = \"expand-to-distinguish.\"** In the review UI, *skip without opening the abstract* is a\n115\t  stage-1 negative; *open the abstract then skip* is a stage-1 positive + stage-2 negative; *keep*\n116\t  after opening is positive for both. This recovers both funnel labels from one interface\n117\t  (`feedback.derive_labels()`). Decisions never touch the ground-truth CSVs — only `state/feedback.jsonl`.\n118\t- **Download = separate post-filter step.** `recsys.download` reads the keeps from `state/feedback.jsonl`\n119\t  (latest decision per ID wins — re-keeping resurfaces, a later skip drops it) and pulls PDFs into\n120\t  `pdfs-to-summarize/`, the folder `newsletter-podcast.py` already consumes. Filenames use the legacy\n121\t  `{title}.pdf` scheme so they dedup against anything grabbed the old way; existing files are skipped,\n122\t  so it's safe to re-run as you work through a backlog. Review is offline; only this step hits arXiv.\n123\t- **arXiv fetch gotchas:** (1) the `arxiv` library sets no socket timeout, so a stalled connection\n124\t  hangs forever — `ArxivClient(timeout=...)` installs a process-wide one. (2) Big backlogs must be\n125\t  date-windowed (`--window-days`) — a single sorted query can't deep-page past ~tens of thousands.\n126\t  (3) `search()` retries a flaky empty *first* page (the library raises `UnexpectedEmptyPageError`)\n127\t  but keeps partial results when the empty page is just the end-of-window boundary. (4) **HTTP 429 =\n128\t  rate-limited.** arXiv throttles aggressively under heavy use; the client aborts loudly on 429\n129\t  rather than hammering. Run big backlogs with a generous `--delay` (5–10s) and off-peak. A windowed\n130\t  run **checkpoints each completed window** (`state/backlog.json` + `backlog_candidates.jsonl`), so a\n131\t  re-run of the same command resumes and skips finished windows — that, *not* the abstract cache, is\n132\t  what makes a resume cheap (search results carry abstracts inline, so the cache saves no requests).\n133\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rm4EZvccVjfcRX2TcwGjnC","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/arxiv-summaries-workflow","dirty_fingerprint":"3f7c63b121e23d4c0015b606cbe53718565b5e5296f88904cbd24ec0d96de854","head":"4de35a5867b691d0820dce9f96716410195ab0a7","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/arxiv-summaries-workflow.git"},"id":"ev2-4f1966d75f816c2c269de2fcca119c23432607dfe472128c65223d5c32fcfc1e","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"a