{"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=68\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[project]\nname = \"recsys\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"arXiv paper recommender: cascade title/abstract ranker over a frozen embedding backbone\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.10\"\ndependencies = [\n    \"arxiv==2.1.3\",\n    \"pandas>=2.2,<3\",\n    \"pyarrow>=15\",\n    \"numpy>=1.26,<3\",\n    \"requests>=2.31\",\n    \"sentence-transformers>=3,<6\",\n    \"scikit-learn>=1.4\",\n]\n\n[tool.setuptools]\npackages = [\"recsys\"]\n---\n\"\"\"Incremental-inference state: a seen-set and a run watermark.\n\nThe recommender runs on-demand with gaps of ~1 week to ~3 months. To avoid\nre-recommending papers across runs we persist:\n\n- ``state/seen_ids.txt`` — every arXiv ID we have *scored* (not just downloaded),\n  one per line. Membership test drives candidate filtering.\n- ``state/last_run.json`` — the watermark (latest ``paper_date`` we've scored) and\n  bookkeeping, so the next incremental fetch knows where to resume.\n\nBoth are plain text/JSON so they're trivially inspectable and git-diffable.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nREPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nSTATE_DIR = REPO_ROOT / \"state\"\nSEEN_IDS_PATH = STATE_DIR / \"seen_ids.txt\"\nLAST_RUN_PATH = STATE_DIR / \"last_run.json\"\n\n\ndef load_seen_ids(path: str | Path = SEEN_IDS_PATH) -> set[str]:\n    \"\"\"Load the set of already-scored arXiv IDs (empty set if file absent).\"\"\"\n    p = Path(path)\n    if not p.exists():\n        return set()\n    with p.open(\"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        return {line.strip() for line in f if line.strip()}\n\n\ndef add_seen_ids(ids, path: str | Path = SEEN_IDS_PATH) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Union ``ids`` into the on-disk seen-set; returns the count of new IDs added.\n\n    Idempotent: re-adding known IDs is a no-op. Rewrites the file sorted so diffs\n    stay readable.\n    \"\"\"\n    p = Path(path)","is_error":false,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G7YTScSWJKj59qv8nWqtMa","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/arxiv-summaries-workflow","dirty_fingerprint":"3f7c63b121e23d4c0015b606cbe53718565b5e5296f88904cbd24ec0d96de854","head":"4de35a5867b691d0820dce9f96716410195ab0a7","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/arxiv-summaries-workflow.git"},"id":"ev2-2e9a674ac8465fa38c3eb43cb39c602b01615c4ac4c84939c4edd901dfad89d4","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"session_id":"eb608668-7a33-49bd-9512-90665e51d828","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.228"},"occurred_at":"2026-08-12T01:37:31.095Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/arxiv-summaries-workflow","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=68\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[project]\nname = \"recsys\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"arXiv paper recommender: cascade title/abstract ranker over a frozen embedding backbone\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.10\"\ndependencies = [\n    \"arxiv==2.1.3\",\n    \"pandas>=2.2,<3\",\n    \"pyarrow>=15\",\n    \"numpy>=1.26,<3\",\n    \"requests>=2.31\",\n    \"sentence-transformers>=3,<6\",\n    \"scikit-learn>=1.4\",\n]\n\n[tool.setuptools]\npackages = [\"recsys\"]\n---\n\"\"\"Incremental-inference state: a seen-set and a run watermark.\n\nThe recommender runs on-demand with gaps of ~1 week to ~3 months. To avoid\nre-recommending papers across runs we persist:\n\n- ``state/seen_ids.txt`` — every arXiv ID we have *scored* (not just downloaded),\n  one per line. Membership test drives candidate filtering.\n- ``state/last_run.json`` — the watermark (latest ``paper_date`` we've scored) and\n  bookkeeping, so the next incre